    <statement><p>Write the mixed number as a decimal number.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{4{\textstyle\frac{17}{25}}}</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{4{\textstyle\frac{11}{16}}}</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.68</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.6875</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To change a fraction to decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator. We can simply copy over the integer part of a mixed number.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{4{\textstyle\frac{17}{25}}} = 4 + 17 \div 25 = 4.68</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{4{\textstyle\frac{11}{16}}} = 4 + 11 \div 16 = 4.6875</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
